.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt X509_GET_SUBJECT_NAME 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm X509_NAME_hash_ex ,
.Nm X509_NAME_hash ,
.Nm X509_get_subject_name ,
.Nm X509_set_subject_name ,
.Nm X509_subject_name_hash ,
.Nm X509_get_issuer_name ,
.Nm X509_set_issuer_name ,
.Nm X509_issuer_name_hash ,
.Nm X509_REQ_get_subject_name ,
.Nm X509_REQ_set_subject_name ,
.Nm X509_ACERT_get0_issuerName ,
.Nm X509_ACERT_set1_issuerName ,
.Nm X509_CRL_get_issuer ,
.Nm X509_CRL_set_issuer_name
.Nd get X509_NAME hashes or get and set issuer or subject names
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/x509.h
.Ft unsigned long
.Fo X509_NAME_hash_ex
.Fa "const X509_NAME *x"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fa "int *ok"
.Fc
.Ft X509_NAME *
.Fo X509_get_subject_name
.Fa "const X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_set_subject_name
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fa "const X509_NAME *name"
.Fc
.Ft unsigned long
.Fo X509_subject_name_hash
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft X509_NAME *
.Fo X509_get_issuer_name
.Fa "const X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_set_issuer_name
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fa "const X509_NAME *name"
.Fc
.Ft unsigned long
.Fo X509_issuer_name_hash
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft X509_NAME *
.Fo X509_REQ_get_subject_name
.Fa "const X509_REQ *req"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_REQ_set_subject_name
.Fa "X509_REQ *req"
.Fa "const X509_NAME *name"
.Fc
.Ft X509_NAME *
.Fo X509_CRL_get_issuer
.Fa "const X509_CRL *crl"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_CRL_set_issuer_name
.Fa "X509_CRL *x"
.Fa "const X509_NAME *name"
.Fc
.In openssl/x509_acert.h
.Ft X509_NAME *
.Fo X509_ACERT_get0_issuerName
.Fa "const X509_ACERT *x"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_ACERT_set1_issuerName
.Fa "X509_ACERT *x"
.Fa "const X509_NAME *name"
.Fc
The following macro has been deprecated since OpenSSL 3.0, and can be
hidden entirely by defining
.Ar OPENSSL_API_COMPAT
with a suitable version value, see
.Xr openssl_user_macros 7 :
.Fd #define X509_NAME_hash(x) X509_NAME_hash_ex(x, NULL, NULL, NULL)
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn X509_NAME_hash_ex
returns a hash value of name
.Fa x
or 0 on failure, using any given library context
.Fa libctx
and property query
.Fa propq .
The
.Fa ok
result argument may be NULL or else is used to return 1 for success and
0 for failure.
Failure may happen on malloc error or if no SHA1 implementation is
available.
.Pp
.Fn X509_NAME_hash
returns a hash value of name
.Fa x
or 0 on failure, using the default library context and default property
query.
.Pp
.Fn X509_get_subject_name
returns the subject name of certificate
.Fa x .
The returned value is an internal pointer which
.Sy MUST NOT
be freed.
.Fa x
.Sy MUST NOT
be NULL.
.Pp
.Fn X509_set_subject_name
sets the issuer name of certificate
.Fa x
to
.Fa name .
The
.Fa name
parameter is copied internally and should be freed up when it is no
longer needed.
.Pp
.Fn X509_subject_name_hash
returns a hash value of the subject name of certificate
.Fa x .
.Pp
.Fn X509_get_issuer_name ,
.Fn X509_set_issuer_name ,
and
.Fn X509_issuer_name_hash
are identical to
.Fn X509_get_subject_name ,
.Fn X509_set_subject_name ,
and
.Fn X509_subject_name_hash
except they relate to the issuer name of
.Fa x .
.Pp
Similarly
.Fn X509_REQ_get_subject_name ,
.Fn X509_REQ_set_subject_name ,
.Fn X509_ACERT_get0_issuerName ,
.Fn X509_ACERT_set1_issuerName ,
.Fn X509_CRL_get_issuer
and
.Fn X509_CRL_set_issuer_name
get or set the subject or issuer names of certificate requests of CRLs
respectively.
.Pp
Since attribute certificates do not have a subject name, only the issuer
name can be set.
For details on setting X509_ACERT holder identities, see
.Xr X509_ACERT_set0_holder_entityName 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn X509_get_subject_name ,
.Fn X509_get_issuer_name ,
.Fn X509_REQ_get_subject_name
.Fn X509_ACERT_get0_issuerName
and
.Fn X509_CRL_get_issuer
return an
.Vt X509_NAME
pointer.
.Pp
.Fn X509_NAME_hash_ex ,
.Fn X509_NAME_hash ,
.Fn X509_subject_name_hash
and
.Fn X509_issuer_name_hash
return the first four bytes of the SHA1 hash value, converted to
.Sy unsigned long
in little endian order, or 0 on failure.
.Pp
.Fn X509_set_subject_name ,
.Fn X509_set_issuer_name ,
.Fn X509_REQ_set_subject_name ,
.Fn X509_ACERT_get0_issuerName
and
.Fn X509_CRL_set_issuer_name
return 1 for success and 0 for failure.
.Sh BUGS
In case
.Fn X509_NAME_hash ,
.Fn X509_subject_name_hash ,
or
.Fn X509_issuer_name_hash
returns 0 it remains unclear if this is the real hash value or due to
failure.
Better use
.Fn X509_NAME_hash_ex
instead.
